\newlabel{tab:gta_detailed}{{2}{7}{\textbf {Learning to use pre-provided tools on GTA (121-case validation split).} \sysname {} Mode~B (skills~$+$~mastery only; no new tool generation) improves every metric on every backbone and beats both \emph {Base Agent} and the \emph {XSkill-style}~\citep {DBLP:journals/corr/abs-2603-12056} generic-skill-injection baseline. XSkill-style itself drops below Base on the step-level metrics for GPT-4o and GPT-5.4, showing that generic skill injection without environment-specific protocols can confuse tool selection. \relax }{table.caption.22}{}}
